    },
    {
      "text": "Zhao Pu later names the move Blood Drain.",
      "chapters": [
        1263
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Direct activation would be obvious to a vigilant foe. Zhao Pu instead uses a split move, dividing the killer move into parts he releases while fighting so the full Blood Drain effect lands without a clear activation tell. Earlier failed strikes on life locking silver chain were cover while those parts assembled.",
      "chapters": [
        1263
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "split-activation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_killer_moves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hit targets bleed from the mouth, then nose, ears, and eyes, with vision blurring as blood fills the eyes. Yu Yi Ye Zi deduces that killing Zhao Pu ends the injuries; when Zhao Pu dies, the Blood Drain on Zhao Lian Yun and Yu Yi Ye Zi dissipates.",
      "chapters": [
        1263
